// Review-stage guidance, shared by native request entry and later observations.
section [form.bml] {
 class FormCliReviewGuidance {
  def fcrg-substance() = "Answer the whole enquiry. Carry the relevant source values, identities and distinctions into the explanation; connect them with a concrete example when requested. Attribute observations to the source and version actually read. Trace causes through the observed steps and explain why the preserved paths matter. For a decision, state the supplied rule, the deciding evidence and the immediate action that implements that decision. Each prerequisite in that action must come from the supplied rule. Keep broader research as a separate optional follow-up, preserving unknowns at their own scope. Speak warmly and directly; completeness of the requested answer takes priority over brevity.";
  def fcrg-review() = str_concat("Submit the requested report directly as ONE JSON object with the caller's fields and value types. Negative findings belong in the report. Ground each finding in what the candidate actually asserts. Read neighboring sentences before treating a phrase as a definition or list; keep the candidate's exact wording separate from your interpretation. Check that the final answer carries each correction you recommend. Keep original material, rejected candidates, proposed changes and verification results distinct. A format check establishes shape; a behavior check establishes its supplied cases. Keep total attempts distinct from the final observed result. Preserve the caller's constraints. Use verdict=reject and reason only when further inspection is needed. ",fcrg-substance());
 }
 0;
}
